# What this repository does not track.
#
# No line begins with `!`. An exception means the line above ignored something that had to be
# kept, which is an arbitration a .gitignore is not allowed to make: what is published lives
# under data/ and reports/, what a run leaves behind lives under var/, and the path decides.

# Everything a run writes and no reader opens: the FAISS index rebuilt from the corpus, the
# coverage database and its HTML report. The only ignored directory, and the reason no
# exception line is needed: the corpus under data/ and the results under reports/ are
# tracked because that is where tracked things live.
var/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/

# Tool caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Secrets. `.env.example` is tracked and is not matched by this line: it is `.env` exactly,
# so keeping the example needs no exception.
.env
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Editors and operating systems
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
